Numerical Examples
In this section we present several numerical examples to illustrate the theoretical results in the preceding sections. We start in Example REF  by comparing the performance of our policy (REF ) to that of the standard finite horizon LQG controller whenever the control inputs set {{formula:d4490590-b567-4abf-9d3f-40011628fe54}} , i.e., there are no bounds on the norm of the inputs. Then we compare the performance of our policy (REF ) against a saturated LQG controller in Example REF . Finally, in Example REF  we illustrate the effectiveness of our policy (REF ) compared to the certainty-equivalent receding horizon control.
Example 6.1 (Unconstrained Inputs) 

