The present day quantum theories offer some visions of new, mathematically possible reality which, until now, were not experimentally detected. Thus, the idea of supersymmetry looks for particles in superposed states of `being fermion' and `being boson' and for the corresponding invariance group, with consequences for elementary particles, strings, and quantum cosmology {{cite:07c07b0e60de6646a02adb53952c504fad367d69}}, {{cite:debe254f56a9cd2e07bc6bbdb6e26277332f74fd}}, {{cite:17af50ba2f6ca8112485ec7bcb728fd588ca224b}}, {{cite:fee5ab6b95f209d1525d79478739c5a0b105a47a}}, {{cite:c4a3af9b0d0b14d0557325479f20da48c1019840}}, {{cite:5aa1964aac43adf9f9a3b51a5acf72442bf2b974}}. The other models propose to avoid the field singularities by assuming that the very structure of the physical space forbids the exact point localizations. In some of them (Connes, Madore, Bellisard) the physical points have the non-commuting coordinates {{cite:c63b74f3f903e113f28239855417f8f8e2573c3b}}, {{cite:33090ec1989a2584574bf08e898a1213e0e4ab35}}, {{cite:937e95bc17914a1a91d13a838880e2fbe8a1b89a}}, {{cite:70e77be37057ed3ed0077dcca70b65cea84424aa}}, {{cite:1647ef59af1d7631fce138231901bc803dd6026e}}, {{cite:95e4548cea306b3927b30ef7b24dd43cf3837d0c}}, {{cite:7787ab9771f195eb57b985564b33f955f1e09f0d}}, {{cite:eab5e3b9f9f1ac184b91175eeb5f9d42845a6153}}, {{cite:f3ded6f92b76c25e241b9a2d3a25401c7faa7638}}, {{cite:69bf0d9288999ae3924ab8d612448ce1106143e9}}, {{cite:1e6c6f3529814165b95d0b33b6c019414b88056a}}, {{cite:f0b18ab75cc7bf084d421471fee22f1aa67961bf}}, {{cite:8e5d2d79d3f20e3331e88275f9afd1b152809bf8}}. According to Doplicher et al {{cite:da2a94e01d64d85833ca2d176a5f32bf6bc857fc}}, {{cite:4e5e550a35881fff54b01c9b3fd134fb0d333100}}, this might explain why the exact position measurements in the Heisenberg's microscope cannot produce the microscopic black holes, (even if the reality of the danger is an open problem). In the simplest model of the non-commutative plane (Madore {{cite:33090ec1989a2584574bf08e898a1213e0e4ab35}}) the points {{formula:e6f5be36-6ae9-4093-89f8-049810d5198d}}  fulfill {{formula:a4e69edc-edcb-411e-a56e-ca5af77f8dcf}} , preventing as well the singularity creation.

Though all these ideas are just free associations (in almost psychoanalytic sense), no better justified is the traditional hypothesis that our space is indeed a continuum of the `exact points'. In fact, if adopting Wigner's observation about the “unreasonable power of mathematics" {{cite:16fc65b78997025ba28cc8d11968a5321bd7f38d}}, the mathematical models, if correct, must appear somewhere in nature. So indeed happens, but with one amendment. The nature might `use' our models in its own way, without caring about the author's intentions. Thus, while the problem of boson-fermion supersymmetry waits to be solved (still no trace of Higgs boson, no gravitinos, etc.), the same mathematical structure appeared in the supersymmetric quantum mechanics (Witten {{cite:b2dd28b7f5d03cecded29d9f360bba2dbda560d8}}, {{cite:36b2fe5e3d4781c1bbca1570eabc2a51ac3a70d4}}) helping to solve exactly a class of spectral problems (Duplij et al {{cite:5aa1964aac43adf9f9a3b51a5acf72442bf2b974}}). While there is still no sign of strings, branes nor extra dimensions, the analogous mathematical structures permit to understand better certain biological phenomena. In fact, the 'clones' of almost all unborn structures start invading the present day physics forming a little-great science in its own right (c.f. “big-bang in probet” etc. {{cite:fb037c5ede0bfce461fa247b520257cba5bb415b}}, {{cite:00220013952ac4f2231533858410c4d4e0adf11a}}).

Below, we shall discuss a similar status of the `non-commutative points' which appear in the quantum Hall effect. We shall show that the idea works not only for the static fields but also for time dependent ones, even though the more fundamental hypothesis concerning the granular structure of the space itself is still waiting to be confirmed (or abandoned?).

