The disc is a thin, non-magnetic, non-self-graviting, inviscid perfect gas disc which is vertically isothermal. Its radial surface density and temperature are described by power-law profiles. Notations are described in Appendix . The flow is laminar and in stationary equilibrium. Consequently, the gas velocity and density are described by well-known relations, which we present in Appendix .

